From 5f27d43e04642b81b33498b3d2d304b740f5fe40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:42:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add Trustpilot (full auto) and Facebook (fetch-only)
 integrations, Yelp manual entry

Yelp has no public API for reading or replying to reviews (Partner API is invite-only,
aimed at large reputation platforms), and Facebook's Graph API has no reply-posting
endpoint for ratings/recommendations at all -- neither is a gap that permissions or a
different approach can close. Rather than scrape/automate logins against either site
(a real ToS and account-suspension risk for customers, not worth it for this product),
both now flow through the same AI-drafting and safety-check pipeline as Google, just
always held for the owner to copy the reply over by hand instead of auto-posting.

- src/platforms.js: central registry of what each platform (google, trustpilot,
  facebook, yelp) can fetch and auto-post -- draftReply/pollReviews/dashboard all read
  capabilities from here instead of hardcoding platform names
- src/trustpilot.js: fetch (API key) + reply (OAuth business-user token) -- genuinely
  full automation, on par with Google
- src/facebook.js: fetch only (Graph API ratings/recommendations) -- always held
- dashboard.js: new "Add a Yelp review manually" form feeding the same pipeline;
  queue cards now show "Approve & Post" for auto-postable platforms or "Copy Reply &
  Mark Sent" (with clipboard copy) for the rest
- draftReply.js: hold-for-review now also triggers when the platform itself has no
  posting API, independent of star rating or safety-check result
- sql/002_multi_platform.sql: adds reviews.entry_method (api | manual)
